    "media:imagetext": "#1116\nINTERNATIONAL AIRPORT\nEL PASO, TEXAS\nThe conquistadores, traveling north on Camino\nReal in 1536 found the location of \"EL PASO\ndel Norte\" (the Pass of the North) ideal as\na base for searching the southwest. Modern\nday\nexplorers,\nwith\nfun and relaxation\nas\ntheir golden goal, find our city the perfect\nheadquarters for today's pilgrimages of pleas-\nure, be they a few hours or a few days. This\nview shows a modern jet plane with the\nFranklin Mountains in the background.\nColor photo by F. J. Schaaf\n1969 Schaaf Post Card Co.\n→ Schee,\nHIT CARES\nNEW MEXICO\nPublished by Schaaf Post Card Co..\nAlamogordo, New Mexico\nPLACE\nSTAMP\nHERE\n41276\nPost Card\n2015,166.1927",
